<blockquote>
<p>“A great Shadow has departed,&quot; said Gandalf, and then he laughed and the sound was like music, or like water in a parched land; and as he listened the thought came to Sam that he had not heard laughter, the pure sound of merriment, for days upon days without count.”</p>
<div style="text-align: right;">
<p><span style="font-size:0.9em;">J.R.R. Tolkien, <em>The Return of the King</em></span></p>
</div>
</blockquote>
<p>This is an SCP about religion, but not in the way(s) you might expect.</p>
<p>This is an SCP about childlike faith, and the struggle to retain it amid a vortex of depravity. It is also about what happens when you have serious, proximal encounters with that depravity in the communities you trust, and then in yourself.</p>
<p>Whoever you are, and whatever you believe, I hope this feeds you one way or the other.</p>
<p><strong>Inspired by:</strong> Bunyan's <em>The Pilgrim's Progress</em>, Marilynne Robinson's <em>Gilead</em>, Lewis' <em>The Great Divorce</em>, and various real-life experiences.</p>
