<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Paul and Silas are students who enrolled into the SS together in 2012. 4 years later, a disillusioned and hurt Silas posts one SCP spoof to the wiki each midnight, as an iconoclastic anger-venting strategy. These spoofs comprise his (and Paul’s) SS-related creative output over the years, and thus divulge his entire backstory.</p>
<p>Paul finds out that Silas is airing dirty laundry on the Internet, and intercepts him on the fifth day by hogging the SCP-5000 slot, urging restraint and forgiveness.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, in the Foundationverse, the Makarios High School undergoes events that are <em>analogous</em> - but not exact - to Silas’ experiences and thematic concerns. Now normally, when an author posts to the mainsite, their anomaly is realised in the Foundation’s reality (as per the SAS proposal). But <em>Silas’</em> authorial intent is not to populate the SCP wiki with new anomalies, it’s to let off steam. And this steam is realised as - or “transmuted” into - a rampaging, socially-twisted Keter. A Keter that the Foundation can’t catalogue properly, because its containment files - ordained by whatever is in the Database - are Silas’ spoofs.</p>
<p>Paul’s intervention on Friday succeeds in consoling Silas and, in the Foundation’s reality, halting the perverse charity drive through the eagle’s sacrifice. When this fifth and final spoof gets voted off the wiki (SCP-3309), all firsthand data about, and physical evidence of, the anomaly vanishes. In real life, Silas cheers up, and gets a special gift.</p>
<hr />
<p>I didn’t write the WD part with the intent to require prior reading, but YMMV. Thanks for highlighting that.</p>
<p>Do let me know if there’s anything I can do to make it more obvious (if it needs to be)!</p>
